def two_sum(nums: list[int], target: int) -> list[int]:
    seen = {}
    for i, num in enumerate(nums):
        complement = target - num
        if complement in seen:
            return [seen[complement], i]
        seen[num] = i
```

Iterates once, storing each value's index in `seen`. For each number it checks whether its complement was already seen; if so, returns both indices. Otherwise records the current number. O(n) time, O(n) space.
